and processes underlying the control of food selection and nutrient intake.</article-title><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Wurtman</surname><given-names>RJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Wurtman</surname><given-names>JJ</given-names></name></person-group><source>Nutrition and the Brain</source><publisher-loc>New York</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Raven Press</publisher-name><fpage>163</fpage><lpage>221</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0004126-Day1"><label>20</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Day</surname><given-names>JEL</given-names></name><name><surname>Kyriazakis</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Rogers</surname><given-names>PJ</given-names></name></person-group><year>1998</year><article-title>Food choice and intake: towards a unifying framework of learning and feeding motivation.</article-title><source>Nutrition Research Reviews</source><volume>11</volume><fpage>25</fpage><lpage>43</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">19087458</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0004126-Dominy1"><label>21</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dominy</surname><given-names>NJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Lucas</surname><given-names>PW</given-names></name><name><surname>Osorio</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Yamashita</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name></person-group><year>2001</year><article-title>The sensory ecology of primate food perception.</article-title><source>Evolutionary Anthropology</source><volume>10</volume><fpage>171</fpage><lpage>186</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0004126-DErchia1"><label>22</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>D'Erchia</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name><name><surname>Gissi</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Pesole</surname><given-